Z||000000||Mach10||09-15-2001||05:58 PM||||News reports say that the Taliban movement is saying that Bin-Laden had nothing to do with the attack. This is interesting. Besides our own personal viewpoints, the FBI and federal government in the states are saying that Bin Laden is at the top of thier lists. What makes this interesting is that the Taliban is saying that they will cooperate FULLY with the US military in apprehending the actual culprit. However, in the same sentence, they also say that they will retaliate if any action is taken towards Bin-Laden or his people. <P>This should prove interesting. If the US ends up going to war with the Taliban, there is going to be guts all over the place. On the bright side, at least the US would have someone to shoot at. <P>The sad part about the Taliban, is that the main fighting force is made up of militia-type peasants. Goat-herders with assault rifles. Most of them cannot read, and have been taught everything they know by a drooling maniac spouting religious dogma about how evil the West is. Most of these people have never even HEARD the Qua'Ran spoken to them in it's intirety. Mostly just snippets of vague passages that could be interpreted in any way that the reader would like.<P>Currently, I am reading a translation of the Qua'ran. It's actually quite interesting. It's pretty much a copy of the "Old Testament" from christianity and judaism. Difference is, it seems to be MUCH more forgiving than our bible... Hear that Eds? I was right. Islam DOES teach tolerance and peace. I'll be writing a short essay on my findings in the next day or so, after I harvest some more choice passages. I'm only like 1/16th through it. This scripture is LONG. Plus I don't read Arabic so well  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||4
