Z||000002||Mach10||09-15-2001||06:26 PM||||Actually, they are doing fairly well with a badly trained, poorly equiped army. They won't pose much of a threat to the US (other than terrorist-type attacks), but they WILL be hard to hit, since most of them will scatter to the hills at the first sign of a properly mounted defence. It's not that they are really strong, it's that they are good at taking over, and holding, lots of small villages while they build their numbers. They are more of a dogmatic virus than an army. They spread, they don't expand  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/tongue.gif"><P>The Taliban wasn't behind this attack, but it looks like they may be supporting/protecting those that were. If this is the case, then 14-year-olds with guns or not, they must be put down. Although morally hard to do, there really is no choice but to take direct action against children with guns, too  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P>That's the sad part  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">||||reg||3
